g b = not b
main = if g (Normal == 0.5) then 2 else 1
-- `if not (Normal == 0.5) then 2 else 1` with the negation behind a helper.
-- The IfThenElse rule derives the False weight as the complement of the True
-- weight; the True weight of the negated equality is the mass 1, so the
-- complement is the mass 0 and the equality's density convention is lost:
-- p(1) answers impossible. The bare `not` is fixed by swapping the arms (task
-- null-set-conventions-not-preserved-under-negation); a negation behind a
-- call, a binding (`(\z -> not z) (Normal == 0.5)`) or a projection (`fst
-- (not (Normal == 0.5), 1)`) is not. The idealized row is the un-negated
-- spelling's. Verified on dev at the fix of that task, interpreter. Docs task
-- if-complement-drops-hidden-negation-density.
